From 11e99d7e0e1e599cea4d34d24c5f8622d4898341 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 16:58:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Admin: build the Crankcase Command Center

Expands the existing /admin shell into a full administrative platform with
nine sections: Command Center, Users, Vehicles, Service Guides, Content,
Revenue, Analytics, System Health, and Security/Audit.

Design and data rules held throughout:
- Every figure is queried live from Postgres for the selected period. Nothing
  is hardcoded, estimated or projected.
- Where a data source genuinely does not exist yet (there is no payment
  provider), tiles read "Waiting for data" rather than a zero that would look
  like a measurement.
- Counting happens in the database, not by loading rows into Node and calling
  .length, so the admin scales past a handful of accounts.
- Authorization is re-checked server-side on every page and every route
  handler. Hidden nav items are not a security boundary.

Also adds first-party event capture and error capture (no third-party
analytics or Sentry account required), and an "Ask Crankcase" command bar that
routes recognised questions to real screens and says plainly when it cannot
answer rather than inventing one.

Requires migrations/2026-09-18-admin-command-center.sql to be run first.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
